# React Frontend

## Stack

- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`)
- Routing: `react-router-dom` in `App.tsx`
- Theme: `ThemeContext` + `ThemeToggle` (dark/light)

## Structure

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `api/` | Fetch wrappers (`client.ts`, `words.ts`, `wordSets.ts`, `search.ts`) |
| `types/` | TS interfaces matching API JSON |
| `components/` | Reusable UI (`WordTable`, `SearchBar`, `PaginationControls`, …) |
| `pages/` | Route-level views (`HomePage`, `WordDetailPage`, `WordSetPage`) |
| `hooks/` | Shared hooks (`useDebouncedValue`) |

## API client

- `request<T>(path)` in `api/client.ts` — throws on non-OK
- Use relative paths (`/api/v1/words`) — Vite proxies to Rails

## Style

- Functional components + hooks
- Colocate types in `types/`; keep components presentational where possible
- Tailwind utility classes; global styles in `index.css`
- Match existing component naming and file layout

## Commands (in `frontend` container)

```bash
docker compose exec frontend npm run dev
docker compose exec frontend npm run build
```
